{"key":"enterprise/T1070.010","id":"T1070.010","name":"Relocate Malware","domain":"enterprise","level":"subtechnique","parent_id":"T1070","tactics":["stealth"],"platforms":["Linux","macOS","Network Devices","Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","network-infrastructure","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Once a payload is delivered, adversaries may reproduce copies of the same malware on the victim system to remove evidence of their presence and/or avoid defenses. Copying malware payloads to new locations may also be combined with File Deletion to cleanup older artifacts. Relocating malware may be a part of many actions intended to evade defenses. For example, adversaries may copy and rename payloads to better blend into the local environment…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1070/010","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--cc36eeae-2209-4e63-89d3-c97e19edf280","source_modified":"2026-05-12T15:12:00.717Z","source_object_version":"2.0","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0064","name":"Command Execution","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0064","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--685f917a-e95e-4ba0-ade1-c7d354dae6e0","page":"telemetry/DC0064/"},{"id":"DC0039","name":"File Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0039","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--2b3bfe19-d59a-460d-93bb-2f546adc2d2c","page":"telemetry/DC0039/"},{"id":"DC0040","name":"File Deletion","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0040","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--e905dad2-00d6-477c-97e8-800427abd0e8","page":"telemetry/DC0040/"},{"id":"DC0061","name":"File Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0061","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--84572de3-9583-4c73-aabd-06ea88123dd8","page":"telemetry/DC0061/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0439","name":"Detection of Malware Relocation via Suspicious File Movement","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0439","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--3fa3299e-a8c2-4555-890b-544314ae1e44","relationship_id":"relationship--3008ab46-7c87-49dd-9c56-aa66c54b80af"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN1216","name":"Analytic 1216","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0439#AN1216","guidance":"Detects the relocation of malicious executables via copy/move actions across suspicious folders (e.g., from Downloads to System32), followed by deletion of the original source or renaming to blend into legitimate binaries.","platforms":["Windows"],"strategy_id":"DET0439"},{"id":"AN1217","name":"Analytic 1217","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0439#AN1217","guidance":"Detects binary movement or copying between untrusted and trusted paths (e.g., /tmp/ → /usr/bin/ or /etc/init.d/) that may indicate persistence attempts or cleanup of origin traces.","platforms":["Linux"],"strategy_id":"DET0439"},{"id":"AN1218","name":"Analytic 1218","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0439#AN1218","guidance":"Detects movement of binaries to `~/Library/`, `/System/`, or app bundle locations, especially after initial execution or download from Safari or Mail.","platforms":["macOS"],"strategy_id":"DET0439"},{"id":"AN1219","name":"Analytic 1219","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0439#AN1219","guidance":"Detects firmware or script relocation attempts (e.g., CLI-based `copy`, `move`, or `rename`) between temporary partitions and config startup folders on routers or switches.","platforms":["Network Devices"],"strategy_id":"DET0439"}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0039","component":"File Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=11","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN1216","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0439#AN1216","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0039/"},{"component_id":"DC0040","component":"File Deletion","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon